        "original_id": "bfe863d1-4f26-534d-8462-5774f12181d0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Benjamin Hanby, Emily Huntington Miller\n- Songs: Jolly Old Saint Nicholas, Up on the Housetop\n- Topics: Christmas music, song authorship attribution\n\nFacts:\n- Benjamin Hanby was born on July 22, 1833, and he was an American composer, educator, and pastor.\n- Emily Huntington Miller was born in 1833 and died in 1913.\n- In December 1865, Emily Huntington Miller published the poem \"Lilly's Secret\" in The Little Corporal Magazine, and that poem originated the Christmas song \"Jolly Old Saint Nicholas.\"\n- In the 1860s, Benjamin Hanby wrote the similar song \"Up on the Housetop.\"\n- The lyrics of \"Jolly Old Saint Nicholas\" have also been attributed to Benjamin Hanby.\n- Benjamin Hanby wrote approximately 80 songs.\n- Benjamin Hanby died on March 16, 1867.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ece77f37-ed03-5e7a-a99d-940e4cc42e87",
        "text": "Page: Benjamin Hanby. Sentence: Benjamin Russell Hanby (July 22, 1833 – March 16, 1867), also given as Benjamin Russel Hanby, was an American composer, educator, and pastor who wrote approximately 80 songs.\nPage: Jolly Old Saint Nicholas. Sentence: \"Jolly Old Saint Nicholas\" is a Christmas song that originated with a poem by Emily Huntington Miller (1833-1913), published as \"Lilly's Secret\" in \"The Little Corporal Magazine\" in December 1865.\nPage: Jolly Old Saint Nicholas. Sentence: The song's lyrics have also been attributed to Benjamin Hanby, who wrote a similar song in the 1860s, Up on the Housetop.",
